    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d218-a2">

                <pb facs="0479" n="409" xml:id="pg409"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2 in No. 446.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Lister to Mr.
                            Lowell.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Foreign Office</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1882-11-16"><hi rendition="#italic">November</hi> 16,
                        1882</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have received your communication of the
                    3d instant stating that it is the wish of Mr. Corcoran, a United States citizen,
                    that the body of the American poet, J. H. Payne, now interred at Tunis, should
                    be exhumed and removed to the United States for reinterment, and I have the
                    honor to state to you in reply that I have caused instructions to be addressed
                    to Her Majesty’s consul-general at Tunis in the sense indicated in your
                    communication now under reply.</p>
                <p>Upon learning the result of Mr. Reade’s application to the Tunisian authorities,
                    I shall address a further communication to you on the subject.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>T. V. LISTER,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">For Earl
                        Granville.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
